## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/h24/lv.png" alt="Latvia" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', marginRight: '8px'}} />Latvia

Latvia stands as one of NATO's most exposed and institutionally integrated frontline states, having undergone the most rapid security transformation in Europe since Russia's 2022 invasion. The country of 1.8 million people is spending nearly 5% of GDP on defense while hosting a 3,500-strong multinational NATO brigade, yet faces a demographic death spiral having lost 30% of its population since 1990. Latvia has achieved maximum institutional lock-in across Western frameworks with zero hedging toward alternative powers, making defection structurally impossible without state collapse. The society remains internally fractured along ethnic lines with 25-30% Russian-speaking population increasingly marginalized through language and citizenship policies, while coalition governments exhibit chronic instability with 17 prime ministers in 33 years. Latvia's strategic culture, forged by occupation memory and deportation trauma, produces extraordinary alliance commitment but operates under mounting fiscal and demographic pressures.

**Key developments:**

- **Security:** Defense ministers Sprūds and Kosiniak-Kamysz discussed joint military exercises, Polish regular presence in Latvia, joint procurement, and continued drone coalition cooperation during Sprūds's Warsaw visit *([tvnet.lv](https://tvnet.lv/8401123/latvijas-un-polijas-aizsardzibas-ministri-apspriez-iespeju-rikot-vienotas-militaras-macibas), 2026-01-21)*
- **Economic:** PM Siliņa announced 260 million euro budget allocation for Rail Baltica implementation, emphasizing need to accelerate construction tempo and seek additional EU funding from new multiannual budget with increased transport sector financing *([tvnet.lv](https://www.tvnet.lv/8402171/silina-sogad-rail-baltica-projekta-istenosanai-paredzeti-260-miljoni-svarigi-kapinat-buvdarbu-tempu), 2026-01-23)*
- **Economic:** PM Siliņa acknowledged possibility of additional state funding for national airline, noting company is seeking private partners while government considers various capital raising options including potential IPO *([delfi.lv](https://www.delfi.lv/bizness/37264250/biznesa_vide/120103672/papildu-valsts-nauda-airbaltic-nav-izslegta-neslepj-silina), 2026-01-22)*
- **Institutional:** Cabinet decided to implement European Media Freedom Act requirements into national legislation, modifying two media regulation laws to ensure transparency in state advertising funding to media outlets *([Government Cabinet](https://www.mk.gov.lv), 2026-01-20)*
- **Domestic:** PM Siliņa acknowledged coalition disagreements after ZZS voted with opposition parties to pass controversial compensation law amendments, leading New Unity to request presidential veto. President Rinkēvičs returned legislation to Saeima for reconsideration *([tvnet.lv](https://www.tvnet.lv/8399682/silina-valdosas-koalicijas-darba-pastav-jautajumi-par-kuriem-partneriem-ir-atskirigi-viedokli), 2026-01-19)*

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **President Rinkēvičs participates in Davos World Economic Forum, discusses Ukraine and Greenland** — President Edgars Rinkēvičs attended the World Economic Forum in Davos from January 19-22, participating in discussions about Ukraine's EU membership and commenting on Trump's Greenland statements. He also expressed support for UN reform and Trump's Peace Council initiative. *([eng.lsm.lv](https://eng.lsm.lv/article/politics/president/19.01.2026-president-rinkevics-departs-for-davos.a630547/))*
- **Saeima reduces administrative burden by eliminating separate job seeker status** — Parliament passed amendments in third reading to eliminate the separate job seeker status to reduce administrative burden on the State Employment Agency while maintaining existing benefits. *([tvnet.lv](https://tvnet.lv/8401594/saeima-mazina-nva-administrativo-slogu-atsakoties-no-darba-mekletaja-statusa))*
- **President commemorates 1991 Barikādes anniversary** — President Rinkēvičs marked the anniversary of the 1991 Barikādes (barricades), emphasizing that the state is not just borders and buildings but people, and noting that 35 years later, Latvia's society remains a powerful force. *([tvnet.lv](https://tvnet.lv/8399917/barikades-atgadina-ka-valsts-nav-tikai-robezstabi-ekas-un-lozungi-uzsver-prezidents))*
- **Border guard accused of illegal electronic cigarette sales** — The Internal Security Bureau recommended prosecution of a State Border Guard officer for illegal sales of electronic cigarettes not marked with Latvian excise tax stamps. *([tvnet.lv](https://tvnet.lv/8402233/rosina-apsudzet-robezsargu-par-elektronisko-smekesanas-iericu-nelikumigu-tirgosanu))*
</Accordion>


